      "message": "fix(xtask): pin the env that enters the cargo unit hash for gate steps\n\nCargo 1.100 gives each workspace unit its own directory\ntarget/<profile>/build/<package>/<hash>/, and the hash covers the profile.\nAgents ran gates in the shared build worktree with and without\nCARGO_INCREMENTAL=0, so each run got a new profile hash and wrote about\n600 new camcraft-app units (~190 MB each). Cargo never removes the old ones.\n\nEvery cargo call of a gate now gets CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 and loses the\ncaller's CARGO_PROFILE_* and CARGO_BUILD_INCREMENTAL variables\n(xtask/src/unit_env.rs). The gate prints the pin, notes a set RUSTFLAGS,\nand its summary prints how many unit directories the run added.\n\nFixes #3150\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
